  "worked_solution": "First, we write $4\\,\\frac{1}{2}$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n4\\,\\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{(4\\times 2)+1}{2}=\\frac{9}{2}\n$$\n\nWe also write $1\\,\\frac{3}{4}$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n1\\,\\frac{3}{4}=\\frac{(1\\times 4)+3}{4}=\\frac{7}{4}\n$$\n\nNow, we can multiply the two numbers. We multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{9}{2}\\times \\frac{7}{4}=\\frac{9\\times 7}{2\\times 4}=\\frac{63}{8}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing number is $63.$",
